comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T14:42:31.427Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status searches for npm 12,npm pack,package install,tarball,and pack output shape found package-lifecycle ancestors and related closed incidents but no item owning the npm 12 object-form receipt plus fail-closed fallback defect. GitHub issue #1136 is therefore net-new canonical work."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:23.293Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: extension package regressions passed; packed npm and Bun consumers installed the generated tarball and executed the CLI and SDK; npx packed smoke passed; full coverage passed exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:16.274Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: npm pack selection now requires a named candidate to match the requested package and permits sole-candidate fallback only when the receipt omits a name. Conflicting-name negative controls, packed npx, npm install, Bun install, Node SDK, Bun SDK, and CLI contracts all pass."
  "2026-08-29T08:19:34.059Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: alias@file specs pass the alias as expected receipt package name although npm pack reports the target manifest name. Reopened for alias-aware selection and a runner regression."
  "2026-08-29T08:23:19.096Z","harness:codex","TDD review fix: reproduced npm file-alias receipt rejection with an isolated npm runner and a keyed receipt whose manifest name differs from the alias. Alias normalization now disables registry-name binding while preserving exact-name validation for unchanged registry specs; focused security and context suites pass."
  "2026-08-29T08:44:05.446Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: npm registry and file-alias receipt regressions pass; strict static quality passed; full suite passed 586 files and 8,115 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; linked PM acceptance passed with zero failures."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T23:24:37.938Z","harness:codex","After a machine-readable subprocess receipt parses successfully, an unsupported shape is a contract error. Falling back to display lines at that point converts structured incompatibility into unsafe filenames."
  "2026-08-29T08:44:05.939Z","harness:codex","An npm file alias names the request, not necessarily the packed manifest. After local alias normalization, bind a keyed receipt by cardinality and validated artifact metadata instead of the alias label; unchanged registry specs retain exact-name binding."
